WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.820
SPEAKER: Let's get
started with Coursera.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.680
The architecting with
Google Cloud Platform

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.935
specialization on Coursera
comprises six courses as shown.

00:00:08.935 --> 00:00:10.560
When your email
address has been added,

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.210
you will get an
invitation email.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.960
To start learning on Coursera,
open the Google Cloud Coursera

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.480
invitation email.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.580
The email has the subject
line, "Join the Associate Cloud

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.220
engineer track offered
by Google Cloud."

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.160
In the email, click "Join Now"
to join the Associate Cloud

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.090
engineer track.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.850
You will then create or sign
into your Coursera account

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.430
and agree to join the program.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.220
Enroll in the first course,
Google Cloud Platform

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.230
Fundamentals core
infrastructure.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.770
Courses have videos, hands
on Qwiklabs, and quizzes.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.800
The courses provide an in-depth
explanation of key concepts

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.850
through videos.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.190
You then learn to apply
the concepts by practicing

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.848
with hands on labs.

00:00:51.848 --> 00:00:53.640
Here's my colleague
Philip Meyer giving you

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.413
an overview of Qwiklabs.

00:00:55.413 --> 00:00:56.830
PHILIPP MAIER:
Hello, and welcome.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.122
I'm Philipp Maier, a course
developer with Google Cloud

00:00:59.122 --> 00:01:00.030
Platform.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.870
And this is a brief tutorial on
using Qwiklabs in this course.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.760
I'm about to show you
the interactive hands

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.860
on labs platform
called Qwiklabs,

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.310
which is part of Google Cloud.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.040
Qwiklabs allows you to get
practical hands on experience

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.950
with GCP and provisions you
with Google account credentials

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.950
so you can access a
GCP console at no cost.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.260
The first step is
to log into Coursera

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.300
in an incognito window.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.890
Depending on your
browser, it may also

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:31.080
be called private browsing
or InPrivate browsing.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.420
Logging into Coursera
from a private window

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.890
ensures that you
don't accidentally

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.710
use your own Google account
while accessing the Google

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.120
Cloud console.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.070
We don't want you to
get any unexpected bills

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.910
at the end of the month.

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.610
Check out the links below this
video for different browser

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.230
support articles.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:50.470
Once logged into Coursera
using an incognito window,

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:53.440
return to your course and
go to the lab activity page.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:59.630
So if prompted, you want
to accept the honor code,

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.670
and you might even have
to enter your name.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.190
Then you want to click
the "open tool" button

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.930
to open the lab in a new tab.

00:02:09.889 --> 00:02:14.300
So within the new tab, you
can now click "start lab,"

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.493
and you want to wait until the
"lab running" is displayed.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.550
For each lab you will have
a timer in the top right

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.860
with the remaining access time.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.720
Your lab will automatically
end when the timer runs out.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.010
On the left, you have
the connections detail.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.350
Click "open Google
console," and then

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:39.450
sign in with the username
and password provided

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.012
in the connections detail pane.

00:02:42.012 --> 00:02:48.440
So I'm going to copy the
username, paste that in here.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:54.520
I'm also going to take the
password, paste it in here too.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.980
Now Qwiklabs creates a new
account for you each time

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:57.882
you launch a lab.

00:02:57.882 --> 00:03:00.340
Therefore you need to click
through the initial account set

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.810
up windows.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:05.890
So essentially any
to accept this.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:08.070
I don't need to add any
recovery phone number,

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.120
so I can just click done.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.100
I'm going to agree to
the terms and services,

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.570
and I don't need any emails.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:23.170
Now I can verify that I'm
using the Qwiklabs provided

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.260
account and project
within the GCB console.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:32.550
So up here I see the
project ID, and over here I

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.063
can see the username.

00:03:35.063 --> 00:03:36.480
And these are the
same ones that I

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.310
was provided with in the
connections detail pane.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:43.950
You can also see that the
timer is still running.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.950
Now some labs track you work
within the Qwiklabs provided

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.600
GCP project.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.490
If this is enabled,
you'll see a score

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:53.010
in the top right
corner of the window,

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:55.120
as you can see right here.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.520
Your score increases
as objectives are met,

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.910
and you can click on the score
to view the individual steps

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.700
to be scored.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.350
Now that I've
completed the lab, I

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.910
can see my score
has been updated,

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.610
and I'm ready to
click "end lab."

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:13.590
Once I click "end
lab," the Qwiklabs

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.529
provided project and any
resources within that project

00:04:16.529 --> 00:04:17.310
will be deleted.

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:23.490
I can close a Qwiklabs
lab page, and my grade

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:26.580
will be updated with my
lab score in Coursera.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.260
That's it for this tutorial.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.860
Remember to launch Coursera
in an incognito window

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.120
and use the Qwiklabs
provided credentials

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.460
to sign into the GCP console.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.890
Good luck with the labs, and
enjoy the rest of this course.

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:41.560
SPEAKER: To summarize, complete
the architecting with Google

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:44.910
Cloud Platform
specialization on Coursera,

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.850
practice with hands
on labs on Qwiklabs,

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.170
and review related
product documentation.

